# Cold boot with SW1 on -> ROM/RAM test -> IO ERROR 64, then a warm reset.
#
# BRAM has no reset in jtframe_dual_ram, so memory survives the reset pulse
# exactly as it does on hardware. MAME skips the test on a warm boot; we do not,
# and that divergence is what this script exercises.
#
# The boot switch is C040: CMPA $3000 -- the main CPU waits ~0.65s for tri-RAM
# offset 0 to read 0xA6 (and 0x0F to go non-zero), and falls into the self-test
# when that times out. See doc/WARMBOOT_HANDOFF.md.
#
# Verdict is mechanical: the frame dumper only writes a PNG when the image
# changes. Two identical bursts (681..709 and 1450..1478, same deltas) means
# both boots errored; a healthy boot keeps emitting frames to the end.
#
#   FRAMES=1700 ROMS_HOST=~/mameroms ./sim-core.sh shouse blastoff \
#       -dipsw fffe ../blastoff/warmreset.cab

# 1. cold boot with SW1 on -> the self-test runs and fails
750

# 2. warm reset: memory keeps its contents
20 reset

# 3. second boot: does it skip the test, as MAME does?
900
